**1. PDF Analysis & Description:**
The attached PDF contains two scientific articles by Fangjia Lu et al., investigating Nano-11, a dendrimer-like α-D-glucan nanoparticle, as a vaccine adjuvant. Derived from sweet corn phytoglycogen, Nano-11 is positively charged and 70-80 nm in diameter. It effectively adsorbs negatively charged antigens, enhancing their uptake and activation of dendritic cells (DCs) in vitro (increased costimulatory molecules, IL-1β, IL-12p40). In mice, Nano-11 boosts antigen-specific antibody responses comparably to aluminum adjuvant. It induces a transient, localized inflammatory response, primarily recruiting monocytes/macrophages, and efficiently targets antigens to migratory DCs in draining lymph nodes, with minimal systemic distribution. The authors conclude Nano-11 is a safe, effective, and cost-effective adjuvant.

